<section data-analytics-module="{
    &quot;module_name&quot;: &quot;Paragraph&quot;,
    &quot;section_header&quot;: &quot;Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model&quot;
  }">
  <uni-article-paragraph>
    <div><p data-block-key="qhyqb">Today, we’re announcing the next frontier model: Gemini 4 Carbon, our strongest model with state-of-the-art cybersecurity and long horizon capabilities.</p><p data-block-key="d716n">Carbon ranks #1 on the recently updated v5.0 of <a href="https://artificialanalysis.ai/evaluations/artificial-analysis-intelligence-index">Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index</a> at 59. It shows significant gains across coding and agentic tasks as well as across key capabilities critical for cybersecurity defense, landing a firm lead in SEC-bench Pro (88.2%) for finding vulnerabilities, ExploitGym (54.8%) for exploitation, and CWE-bench (71.0%) for patching. On internal benchmarks, Carbon drives a strong uplift in generating secure code, and in live coding environments with our own teams it shows reduced misalignment and fabrication rates.</p><p data-block-key="79agv">Building on <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-argon/">Gemini 4 Argon</a>, which was launched two weeks ago, Carbon illustrates the pace at which we’re pushing the frontier forward. Our researchers and models are working hand in hand to advance capabilities faster, while strengthening our safeguards in tandem.</p><p data-block-key="cvllr">We're taking a deliberate approach to rollout and are actively engaged in the U.S. government’s voluntary process for pre-release model testing. Starting this week, we will make Carbon available to a subset of cyber defenders and will gradually phase access to additional trusted partners through our <a href="https://deepmind.google/fairwind-program/">Fairwind Program</a>. We’re continuing to gather feedback and iterate on guardrails before making Carbon available to developers, businesses, and consumers via our product surfaces as soon as possible.</p><p data-block-key="6dbvg">Gemini 4 Carbon will launch at the same introductory price

<a data-ga4-analytics-superscript-click="" data-tooltip-content-id="footnote-content-1" data-target="inline text" href="#footnote-1" id="footnote-source-1" aria-label="Jump to link reference 1"><sup>1</sup></a>
 as Argon at $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, with cached input tokens priced at 95% off input token price.</p></div>
  </uni-article-paragraph>
</section>

  

  
    

<section data-analytics-module="{
    &quot;module_name&quot;: &quot;Paragraph&quot;,
    &quot;section_header&quot;: &quot;Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model&quot;
  }">
  <uni-article-paragraph>
    <div><h2 data-block-key="qhyqb">Improving coding and reasoning for challenging, long-horizon tasks</h2><p data-block-key="4ktbv">Designed to take on much harder, long-horizon engineering problems, Carbon is built for sustained agentic workflows. Internally, our teams have seen Carbon run for days to persist through dead ends to tackle complex, multi-step engineering tasks like root-causing and patching subtle bugs across large codebases and low-level systems.</p><p data-block-key="2ssod">Building on user feedback, we focused on improving model performance across a variety of domains, including coding, agentic, and scientific tasks, as well as full-stack web development and multimodal understanding. With improved quality of output and artifacts in web development, Carbon jumps +89 elo points to land at #4 (1769) on <a href="https://arena.ai/leaderboard/code/webdev">WebDev Arena</a>.</p></div>
  </uni-article-paragraph>
</section>

  

  
    





  
  
  
  
  

























