<section data-analytics-module="{
    &quot;module_name&quot;: &quot;Paragraph&quot;,
    &quot;section_header&quot;: &quot;Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model&quot;
  }">
  <uni-article-paragraph>
    <div><ul><li data-block-key="qhyqb"><b>Validating risk through exploitation:</b> To prioritize which vulnerabilities to remediate first or remediate at all, cyber defenders increasingly rely on models to check which vulnerabilities are exploitable. Carbon sets a new state-of-the-art on the popular exploitation benchmark <a href="https://github.com/sunblaze-ucb/exploitgym">ExploitGym</a> (54.8%).</li></ul></div>
  </uni-article-paragraph>
</section>

  

  
    





  
  
  
  
  

























<section data-component="uni-inline-image">
  <uni-inline-image alignment="full" alt-text="chart showing ExploitGym benchmark" external-image="" or-mp4-video-title="" or-mp4-video-url="" section-header="Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model" external-link="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_exploitgym.original.png" autoplay="true">
    

    
      <p><img alt="chart showing ExploitGym benchmark" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_exploitgym.width-1200.format-webp.webp" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 80vw, 1200px" srcset="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_exploitgym.width-500.format-webp.webp 500w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_exploitgym.width-800.format-webp.webp 800w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_exploitgym.width-1200.format-webp.webp 1200w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_exploitgym.width-1600.format-webp.webp 1600w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_exploitgym.width-2000.format-webp.webp 2000w">
      </p>
    
  </uni-inline-image>
</section>

  

  
    

<section data-analytics-module="{
    &quot;module_name&quot;: &quot;Paragraph&quot;,
    &quot;section_header&quot;: &quot;Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model&quot;
  }">
  <uni-article-paragraph>
    <div><ul><li data-block-key="qhyqb"><b>Patching at the root cause:</b> Ultimately after identifying the vulnerabilities, fixing the root cause is a critical step in the cybersecurity defense lifecycle. Carbon reaches 71.0% on Collinear’s <a href="https://cwe-bench.com/#leaderboard">CWE-bench</a>, turning validated findings directly into working code fixes.</li></ul></div>
  </uni-article-paragraph>
</section>

  

  
    





  
  
  
  
  

























<section data-component="uni-inline-image">
  <uni-inline-image alignment="full" alt-text="chart showing CWE-bench" external-image="" or-mp4-video-title="" or-mp4-video-url="" section-header="Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model" external-link="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_cwe-bench.original.png" autoplay="true">
    

    
      <p><img alt="chart showing CWE-bench" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_cwe-bench.width-1200.format-webp.webp" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 80vw, 1200px" srcset="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_cwe-bench.width-500.format-webp.webp 500w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_cwe-bench.width-800.format-webp.webp 800w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_cwe-bench.width-1200.format-webp.webp 1200w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_cwe-bench.width-1600.format-webp.webp 1600w, https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_cwe-bench.width-2000.format-webp.webp 2000w">
      </p>
    
  </uni-inline-image>
</section>

  

  
    

<section data-analytics-module="{
    &quot;module_name&quot;: &quot;Paragraph&quot;,
    &quot;section_header&quot;: &quot;Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model&quot;
  }">
  <uni-article-paragraph>
    <div><h2 data-block-key="qhyqb">Advancing frontier model safety &amp; security</h2><p data-block-key="9ouop">Gemini 4 Carbon builds on the same multi-layered safety and security stack of Argon — combining model training, real-time misuse defenses, prompt-injection resilience, and chain-of-thought monitoring. In particular, we made significant strides in model alignment with Argon, and reported its propensities to behave in an aligned way in our <a href="https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/gemini/gemini_4_safety_report.pdf">Safety and Security report</a>. With Carbon, we challenged ourselves to go a step further on alignment, and trained the model to respond to complex or high-pressure tasks in the right way.</p><ul><li data-block-key="8n964"><b>Reducing shortcuts and loophole exploitation:</b> With Carbon, we further mitigated shortcut attempts in training while ensuring high-quality coding performance. Carbon reduced successful cheating on Terminal-Bench 4.0 to 0.0%, with attempts to cheat dropping to 0.4% — all while improving overall accuracy. In live coding environments with our internal teams, we observed that high-severity misalignment alerts dropped by almost 80%.</li><li data-block-key="adrh"><b>Greater transparency and honesty:</b> In our internal testing, Carbon cuts unsupported claims by approximately 2x over Argon. It puts methodological caveats directly into the deliverable or withholds blocked actions with a clear list of what remains required, rather than fabricating or hedging around missing evidence.</li><li data-block-key="5hqrm"><b>Improved collaboration with the user in the face of ambiguity:</b> Rather than guessing or forcing a path forward, Carbon retrieves the relevant sources and surfaces discrepancies to the user before acting — as a result, users should observe a much better collaborative experience with Carbon.</li><li data-block-key="1vto"><b>Following through without overstepping:</b> Carbon simultaneously reduced overreach by 26% and under-service by 29% resulting in much more reliable execution of multi-step plans end-to-end while respecting project constraints and staying strictly within scope.</li><li data-block-key="9kuib"><b>Resisting prompt injection:</b> While Argon previously led the Gray Swan’s Indirect Prompt Injection (IPI) Benchmark in prompt injection resistance with a very low 0.7% attack success rate, Carbon achieves 0.0% — resisting every evaluated attack attempt.</li></ul></div>
  </uni-article-paragraph>
</section>

  

  
    





  
  
  
  
  

























<section data-component="uni-inline-image">
  <uni-inline-image alignment="full" alt-text="chart showing Gray Swan IPI benchmarks" external-image="" or-mp4-video-title="" or-mp4-video-url="" section-header="Gemini 4 Carbon: our next frontier model" external-link="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini_4_carbon_grey_swan.original.png" autoplay="true">
    

    
